+
+## Adding a service
+
+larder runs one database and one web app. A proposal to add a service (cache, search engine, queue, anything with its
+own process to operate) has to show what it does that Postgres cannot, and name two volunteers able to restore it.
+That is not never: the card gateway is outside the repository, because it is a hosted service nobody here has to run.
+
+This came up three times before it was written down. Redis for sessions in 2023 was turned down because only one
+volunteer would have run it ([keep sessions in the database](adr/0001-keep-sessions-in-the-database.md)). Redis for
+Celery, adopted, evicted 300 receipt jobs one Saturday night in March 2025 and only one volunteer could restore it
+([run background jobs on Postgres](adr/0002-run-background-jobs-on-postgres.md)). In October 2025 a proposal to add
+Elasticsearch for pantry item search was replaced with Postgres full-text search once the rule was applied; see
+`notes/issue-70.md`.
